course: dictionary
lesson: 4987
title: Indian: a country, a people, an ocean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indian, with a capital I, names things that come from India, a large country in South Asia. «Indian food» is food from India, and the Indian Ocean is a name for a sea and ocean, not for people. Because it is a name, it always starts with a capital letter.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is meant. In «The 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami, after a magnitude 9.1 earthquake off Sumatra, killed about 230,000 people in 14 countries», the words tsunami and earthquake show that Indian Ocean is a place. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a country, a food, a person, or an ocean?
explain: An Indian is a person from India, so «Many Indians» means many people from India. Older books sometimes used Indian for the native peoples of the Americas, but this is out of date. Today people say Native American or First Nations, or they use the name of the people themselves.
fact: Indian, with a capital I, is a name word: India, Indian, Indians.
fact: India is a large country in South Asia, and it has more people than any other country in the world.
fact: The Indian Ocean lies south of India, between Africa and Australia. It is the third largest ocean.
fact: «Indian food», such as curry, dal and naan, is popular in the UK, Australia, Canada and elsewhere.
fact: Columbus wrongly called the people of the Americas «Indians», because he thought he had reached India.
exercise: «The 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami killed about 230,000 people in 14 countries.» In this sentence, Indian Ocean is | A language | A greeting | A type of curry | *An ocean
exercise: «Namaste», with palms pressed together, is a respectful greeting in India and Nepal. Where does Namaste come from? | *India and Nepal | Africa | Australia | Canada
exercise: Why does Indian start with a capital I? | It is a sad word | It is a long word | It is the first word of a sentence | *It is a name for a country or its people
test: What is an Indian? | *A person from India | A greeting from Africa | A kind of storm | A large ocean
test: «The same kind of storm is called a hurricane in the Atlantic, a typhoon in the Pacific, and a cyclone in the Indian Ocean.» Which ocean is the cyclone in? | *The Indian Ocean | The Atlantic | The Pacific | The Arctic
exam: «The Indian Ocean lies south of India, between Africa and Australia.» Where does the Indian Ocean lie? | Between Canada and Brazil | Inside the Arctic | *South of India, between Africa and Australia | North of Europe
